WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.382
Spark has several join strategies.

00:00:02.382 --> 00:00:06.557
If one side is small, Spark may broadcast it to workers.

00:00:06.557 --> 00:00:11.402
If both sides are large, the data may need to be shuffled by join key.

00:00:11.402 --> 00:00:16.937
A practical habit is to filter rows and select needed columns before a large join,

00:00:16.937 --> 00:00:20.217
as long as doing so preserves the correct logic.

00:00:20.217 --> 00:00:25.567
A shuffle moves data across executors so related keys end up together.

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:31.467
GROUP BY, large joins, and global ORDER BY can trigger expensive shuffles.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:38.007
In distributed systems, moving data is often more costly than evaluating the SQL expression itself,

00:00:38.007 --> 00:00:39.749
so plan around data movement.
